---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Accessibility | Zeta" description="Zeta's commitment to an accessible website experience.">
  <section class="page-hero page-hero-compact"><div class="shell narrow"><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Accessibility</p><h1>An Inclusive Digital Experience</h1><p>Zeta aims to make its website usable across devices and assistive technologies, with a practical target of WCAG 2.2 Level AA where applicable.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell prose"><h2>Current approach</h2><p>The website uses semantic headings, visible keyboard focus, accessible form labels, reduced-motion support, responsive layouts, descriptive link text, and contrast-conscious colors.</p><h2>Feedback</h2><p>Add an approved accessibility contact so visitors can report barriers and request information in another usable format.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
